
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Brett Terpstra has <a href="https://brettterpstra.com/2026/11/04/mermaid-and-mathjax-for-nvalt/">added math and diagram previews to nvALT</a>. Hooray!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The preview now uses MathJax to typeset equations and Mermaid to turn a fenced <code>mermaid</code> block into a diagram. That makes a note containing a formula or flowchart easier to read while you&#8217;re working on it.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Brett says both libraries are bundled with the app and only load when a note needs them. The preview doesn&#8217;t fetch them from a website, so those features can work offline.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Brett has also <a href="https://brettterpstra.com/projects/nvalt/">updated the nvALT project page</a> with the installation instructions and documentation in one place.</p>
